    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership-level rule lived as an inline MapStruct expression in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, capped at `min(3, \u2026)`. To add level 4 (tenure > 365 days) without inflating that expression or the mapper method, I followed the codebase's existing pattern of small cohesive helper classes (`OwnerAgeBand`, `OwnerLocality`, etc.):\n\n- **New** `rest/function/owner/OwnerMembershipLevel.java` \u2014 an isolated final class with a static `of(Owner)` that keeps the pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) capped at 3, then adds 1 only when tenure since `registrationDate` exceeds 365 days.\n- **One line** changed in `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 the `membershipLevel` expression now delegates to `OwnerMembershipLevel.of(owner)`.\n\nA new owner's `registrationDate` is set to today (`BuildOwner`), so tenure is 0 \u2192 the cap holds and a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 lands at level 3, as the spec and `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` require.\n\nStructural impact stays low: the logic sits in a brand-new class with zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), and the only pre-existing function touched is the mapper method via a single-line annotation edit.",
